{
  "service": "erp",
  "action": "post_shipment",
  "componentType": "rest",
  "description": "Complex: legacy IdP token fetch — POST a body, pull the token out of a nested path, send it under a custom header. Password-grant shaped, which RFC 9700 section 2.4 prohibits (MUST NOT be used); this block exists only for IdPs that offer nothing else. Registration-only: jwt.local / jwt.external execution is not implemented yet, so invoking returns 501.",
  "config": {
    "request": {
      "uri": "https://erp.legacy.local/shipments",
      "method": "POST",
      "contentType": "application/json",
      "headers": { "X-Env": "{$context.environment}" },
      "auth": {
        "ssl": { "ca": "{$env.ERP_CA_PEM}" },
        "jwt": {
          "external": {
            "username": "apiconfy-user",
            "password": "{$env.ERP_PASSWORD}",
            "accessTokenUri": "https://erp.legacy.local/auth/token",
            "credentialPlacement": "body",
            "contentType": "application/x-www-form-urlencoded",
            "requestBody": { "grant_type": "password", "audience": "erp-api" },
            "responsePath": "data.accessToken",
            "requestHeader": "X-ERP-Token",
            "tokenPrefix": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "payloadTemplate": { "shipmentId": "{$context.shipmentId}", "carrier": "{$context.carrier}" },
      "validation": {
        "fields": [
          { "path": "shipmentId", "required": true, "type": "string" },
          { "path": "carrier", "required": true, "type": "string" }
        ]
      }
    },
    "timeout": { "response": 15000 },
    "resilience": { "retryCount": 1, "retryDelay": 500, "backoff": "fixed", "retryOn": [502, 503] },
    "output": {
      "validation": { "rules": [{ "expression": "{$output.shipmentId} != null", "message": "shipmentId missing" }] },
      "transformation": { "postShipmentResponse": { "shipmentId": "{$output.shipmentId}", "acceptedAt": "{$output.acceptedAt}" } }
    }
  },
  "condition": "{$context.shipmentId} != null",
  "metaData": { "owner": "logistics-team", "auth": "legacy-token-endpoint" }
}

{
  "service": "partner",
  "action": "sync_catalog",
  "componentType": "rest",
  "description": "Complex: no token endpoint at all — the JWT is signed locally on every call (HS256 here, RS256 also supported) with iss/aud/sub and a 300 s exp. Registration-only: jwt.local / jwt.external execution is not implemented yet, so invoking returns 501.",
  "config": {
    "request": {
      "uri": "https://partner.example.com/catalog/sync",
      "method": "POST",
      "contentType": "application/json",
      "headers": { "X-Request-Id": "{$context.requestId}" },
      "auth": {
        "jwt": {
          "local": {
            "algorithm": "HS256",
            "secretOrPrivateKey": "{$env.PARTNER_JWT_SECRET}",
            "claims": { "issuer": "apiconfy", "audience": "partner-api", "subject": "svc-catalog" },
            "expiresInSeconds": 300,
            "requestHeader": "Authorization",
            "tokenPrefix": "Bearer "
          }
        }
      },
      "payloadTemplate": { "catalogId": "{$context.catalogId}", "full": true },
      "validation": {
        "fields": [
          { "path": "catalogId", "required": true, "type": "string" },
          { "path": "full", "required": true, "type": "boolean" }
        ]
      }
    },
    "timeout": { "response": 8000 },
    "resilience": { "retryCount": 2, "retryDelay": 300, "backoff": "exponential", "retryOn": [502, 503] },
    "output": {
      "validation": { "rules": [{ "expression": "{$output.synced} != null", "message": "synced flag missing" }] },
      "transformation": { "syncCatalogResponse": { "synced": "{$output.synced}", "catalogId": "{$context.catalogId}" } }
    }
  },
  "condition": "{$context.catalogId} != null",
  "metaData": { "owner": "partner-integrations", "auth": "jwt-local" }
}

request.description:
Registration already validates the auth block, but only `basic` and `oauth2` execute; `jwt.local` signing and `jwt.external` are still Phase 4, so invoking a `jwt` block returns NOT_IMPLEMENTED with attempts=0 and no env resolution — the guard runs before dispatch, deliberately: sending the call without its auth header would be worse than refusing.

Expected error envelope:
```json
{
  "error": {
    "code": "NOT_IMPLEMENTED",
    "message": "Configured but not implemented: config.request.auth.jwt",
    "details": {
      "unsupported": [
        { "field": "config.request.auth.jwt", "phase": "Phase 4" }
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

